  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOZ005N ldai Acute Crisis Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tropical Cyclone Idai made landfall north of Beira City in Sofala Province and the cyclone path continued across Mozambique through Manica Province. The cyclone brought torrential rains and winds to Sofala, Zambezia, Manica, Inhambane and Tete provinces, which are most heavily affected by the cyclone&#x2019;s path and preceding tropical depression. CARE proposes a JR programme focused on immediate distributions of shelter and hygiene kits to address urgent needs and help reduce spread of waterborne diseases in the coming weeks. Temporary classrooms will also be constructed. Initial focus on Sofala province but also including flood affected provinces of Manica, Tete and Zambezi. Given the urgency of restoring shelter to affected communities, the distribution of shelter kits will be undertaken over the first few weeks of the response. We expect to have all shelter kits distributed within the first month of the response. Lead in time will be the verifcation of assessments and targeting validation. Once this is completed, COSACA/CARE will commence distributions of shelter, tool and hygiene kits. 
Construction of temporary classrooms will take place following assessment and site safety inspections, in coordination with the education cluster and school authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
